From 007a98ef059258ac9e7eaef82e9d68fb16946add Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Campos Ramos <Capitain_Jack@yahoo.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 02:42:07 -0300
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] fix(vk_native): lay every zone and 2D layer in every view
 of a window declared full side by side

Display zones under the declared full side by side target (twice the window wide) showed
the scene in the left picture only. Measured on Stereo KWin, cube_zones_vk_linux on a
native Wayland window: left eye 82.6 percent of the pixels lit, right eye 0.000. Three
places took the target for one window:

- the Local2D flatten, the zone mask raster and the clip rectangles laid each 2D layer
  and each zone rectangle once, in window pixels, which is the left half of the target.
  They are now laid once in every view (flat content is the same pixels in each picture,
  at the screen); the hardware wish keeps the window's own rectangles and width;
- the zone rectangles were scaled into the tile by tile width over the target's width,
  so a zone came out half as wide and half as far across (a squeezed cube in the left
  eye). The renderer is now given the window's width;
- a full-window zone covers the window's width, not the target's.

A layout that cannot be laid in every view (an authored mask for the 2D content, which
spans the whole target, and 2D content under the 3D, which is the display processor's
backdrop) is kept as the person's problem "layout" through sparky-stereo-problems, once
when the answer changes, and ended when it is laid again.

Measured with the same app: both eyes lit (0.827 and 0.828), the 2D strip identical in
both eyes (0 pixels differ), the 3D zones' cube disparity -4.4 and -1.5 px against -3.8
and -2.2 px read from the app's own two views (the undeclared window), the left eye as
before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

Origin: vendor, Sparky Stereo OS ORDER 58c
Forwarded: not-needed
Comment: Display zones and Local2D layers under the declared full side by side output (our patches 0001 to 0003):
 each is laid once in every view, at the screen; a layout that cannot be is told to the person through
 sparky-stereo-problems (key "layout", message LOCAL6).
Last-Update: 2026-11-10
